# Spectacles 2024 (not SPECS)

This Lens runs on **Spectacles 2024** in Lens Studio 5.15.x. Preview mode: `Spectacles (2024)`.

- Say **Spectacles 2024** in chat and docs. Never call this device Specs or SPECS.
- **SPECS** = the new glasses shipping later. Do not use SPECS 27 APIs here.
- Keep code identifiers unchanged (`SpectaclesInteractionKit`, `Editor.TargetPlatform.Spectacles`, …).

# Official samples

Before changing ASR, TTS, RSG, Fetch, or the Cursor/Claude Mac bridge, read:

https://github.com/specs-devs/samples/tree/5.15.4

Clone with Git LFS (ZIP downloads omit large assets).

| Task | Sample |
|---|---|
| ASR / STT, Gemini Live, OpenAI Realtime, RSG | `AI Playground` (`ASRQueryController.ts`) |
| Voice + coding agents, Mac bridge, Cursor/Claude CLI | `Agent Center` (`VoiceInputController.ts`, `Bridge/`) |
| Agentic RSG / tool calling | `Agentic Playground` |
| Microphone record/playback | `Voice Playback` |
| HTTPS | `Fetch` |

Prefer those patterns over new speech or AI wiring. Full table lives in `AGENTS.md` (below the Lens Studio shipped block).

# How to work (mandatory)

First principles. **Never assume anything.** Preview ≠ Spectacles 2024. Compile ≠ it works on device.

Before changing ASR, grab, LookAt, tracking, camera, or networking:

1. Name the actual SceneObject / component / API. Quote `Support/StudioLib.d.ts` — not a hunch.
2. Diff the last **known-good Spectacles 2024 send** (`git log` / `git diff`). Restore that pattern first.
3. Cross-check **5.15.4 samples/templates** (https://github.com/specs-devs/samples/tree/5.15.4), https://developers.snap.com/spectacles, and this repo’s presets. Copy from working; do not invent.
4. Do not `createComponent` SIK or LookAt on grab roots unless a 5.15.4 sample does it on this hardware.

A fix is not done until the failing **device** log is gone and grab / speech / placement still match the last known-good send. Full rules: `AGENTS.md` → “How to work here”.

# Memtrace

Memtrace is **not available** in this repo. Do not call it, probe for it, or retry it. Skip Memtrace/fleet skills; use files + git + `Support/StudioLib.d.ts` + 5.15.4 samples.
